{
  "name": "hold_back",
  "note": "(anim-rework S6 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced; M5) Holding a guard, moving backwards (the natural direction, about speed 1): short shuffle steps of about 28 cm, feet hip width so they never cross, each foot reaching back toes first and rolling flat, knees bent 18-34 deg, her weight low and behind his, the pelvis level; phase-matched to guard_held_stumble (phase 0: both left feet land behind, duty 0.62), so her left foot steps back as his does. The arms hold the hold contacts (solved per key on his stumble pose). Not mirrored (8 keys: the hands keep their sides). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in); wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. The arms were solved onto the guard's contacts (his clips posed at the game's hold placement: 0.32 m ahead, 0.1 m to her left, his 1.78 m against her 1.68 m) and written as plain angles: edit these numbers directly. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
